Feature: The battlefield view
  On: desktop
  VIEW changes the console to the battlefield view, the screen of a real-time strategy game. It
  is the same screen as the commander app of [[Towers]]. Press VIEW again to go back to the
  screens.

  The battlefield fills the window. It shows the valley in 3D, as your camera sees it from above,
  with the plane in it. The sim renders the picture. For a real flight, `sim001_view` renders the
  real place. The console draws home, the [[mission]] on the plane, the plan, the GUIDED target and
  the ground track on the picture. The plane stands on a line from its shadow, so you can see how
  high it flies.

  The camera starts over the plane. W, A, S and D, or the arrow keys, move the camera. If you put
  the mouse at an edge of the battlefield, the camera moves that way. Q and E turn the camera, and
  the mouse wheel moves it nearer to the ground or further from it. Drag the battlefield to move
  the camera. Space moves the camera back to the plane.

  The map tools work on the battlefield as on the [[tactical map]]. There are two more ways to give
  orders. Right-click a point, and the plane flies there in [[GUIDED]]. Hold Shift and right-click,
  and the point becomes the next waypoint of the plan.

  The bottom bar has the minimap, the card of the plane with the picture of its camera, the flight
  display, and the buttons of the vehicle command screen and the map tools.

  Expectation: VIEW changes to the battlefield
    Given the console view is the screens
    When the operator switches the view
    Then the console view is the battlefield

  Expectation: VIEW again changes back to the screens
    Given the console view is the battlefield
    When the operator switches the view
    Then the console view is the screens

  Expectation: The sim renders the battlefield in 3D
    The sim loads the valley first, and the console shows the plain ground until then.

    Given the console view is the battlefield
    When the operator waits for the battlefield
    Then the battlefield picture in the console is live

  Expectation: The camera starts over the plane
    Given the console view is the screens
    When the operator switches the view
    Then the point of the console's camera is the plane

  Expectation: A right-click on the battlefield flies the plane there
    The plane flies to the point at its current altitude, and then it circles the point.

    Given the console view is the battlefield
    And the vehicle is armed
    When the operator right-clicks the battlefield
    Then the autopilot mode is GUIDED

  Expectation: Shift and a right-click add a waypoint to the plan
    The new waypoint is at the plan altitude.

    Given the console view is the battlefield
    And the plan has 0 items
    When the operator adds a waypoint on the battlefield
    Then the plan has 1 item
    And the newest waypoint is at the plan altitude
